---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import StatusBar from "../components/StatusBar.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
import FeatureRow from "../components/FeatureRow.astro";
import FeatureGrid from "../components/FeatureGrid.astro";
import TerminalDemo from "../components/terminal/TerminalDemo.astro";
import InstallTabs from "../components/InstallTabs.astro";
import { REPO_URL } from "../consts.ts";
---
<Base>
  <Nav />
  <main>
    <Hero />

    <section id="features" class="features container">
      <div class="feat-stream">
        <FeatureRow scene="tabs" accent="running" eyebrow="one window">
          <Fragment slot="title">Every process, <span class="accent">one pane of glass</span>.</Fragment>
          <p>Point rumor at a JSON file and it runs your whole stack at once — database,
          cache, API, frontend — each in its own tab with a full PTY and real ANSI colors.</p>
          <p>A <strong>status dot</strong> on every tab tells you at a glance what is running, starting,
          blocked, or crashed. Restart one with <span class="kbd">r</span>, restart everything with
          <span class="kbd">Ctrl+R</span>, kill with <span class="kbd">k</span>.</p>
        </FeatureRow>

        <FeatureRow scene="deps" accent="pending" eyebrow="ordering">
          <Fragment slot="title">Start things in the <span class="accent">right order</span>.</Fragment>
          <p>Declare what each process waits for and rumor gates the startup for you — a
          <strong>TCP port</strong> opening, a <strong>log line</strong> matching, or a one-shot command
          <strong>exiting 0</strong>.</p>
          <p>Migrations finish before the API boots; the API is reachable before the frontend
          starts. Waiting tabs show exactly which gate they are stuck on, and circular graphs
          are rejected before anything launches.</p>
        </FeatureRow>

        <FeatureRow scene="retry" accent="crashed" eyebrow="resilience">
          <Fragment slot="title">Crashes <span class="accent">restart themselves</span>.</Fragment>
          <p>Give a process a retry policy and rumor brings it back when it falls over —
          with <strong>fixed</strong>, <strong>linear</strong>, or <strong>exponential</strong> backoff and an
          optional delay cap.</p>
          <p>The budget resets when you restart by hand, and a deliberate <span class="kbd">k</span>
          never counts as a failure. When the budget runs out, the tab says so plainly.</p>
        </FeatureRow>

        <FeatureRow scene="focus" accent="focus" eyebrow="interactive">
          <Fragment slot="title">Type straight <span class="accent">into any process</span>.</Fragment>
          <p>Press <span class="kbd">Enter</span> to focus a tab and your keystrokes go right to that
          process's PTY — drive a REPL, answer a prompt, poke a dev server. The selected tab and the
          mode indicator turn yellow so you always know input is being forwarded.</p>
          <p>Press <span class="kbd">Esc</span> to step back out to navigation. It is a real terminal,
          not a log viewer.</p>
        </FeatureRow>

        <FeatureRow scene="ports" accent="info" eyebrow="dynamic ports">
          <Fragment slot="title">No more <span class="accent">port collisions</span>.</Fragment>
          <p>Name the port variables you need and rumor allocates free ports once per checkout,
          persists them to <span class="kbd">.rumor-ports.json</span>, and feeds them into commands,
          args, and dependency checks via <span class="kbd">${"{PORT}"}</span>.</p>
          <p>Every <strong>git worktree</strong> gets its own ports, so you can run three branches of the
          same app side by side without touching a config.</p>
        </FeatureRow>

        <FeatureRow scene="logs" accent="waiting" eyebrow="logs">
          <Fragment slot="title">Every line, <span class="accent">captured & searchable</span>.</Fragment>
          <p>Scroll back through any tab, search with a regex using <span class="kbd">/</span>, jump
          between matches, and toggle line-wrap with <span class="kbd">w</span>.</p>
          <p>Everything is mirrored to a plain-text session log on disk. Copy the path with
          <span class="kbd">y</span> to grep it, tail it, or hand it to a teammate. Old sessions clean
          themselves up.</p>
        </FeatureRow>

        <FeatureRow scene="raw" accent="running" eyebrow="agents & pipes">
          <Fragment slot="title">Built for <span class="accent">agents and pipelines</span>.</Fragment>
          <p>Add <span class="kbd">--raw</span> and rumor skips the TUI entirely: one combined stdout,
          one <span class="kbd">[name]</span>-prefixed line per process, ANSI stripped by default.</p>
          <p>Narrow it with <span class="kbd">--only api,web</span>, keep color with
          <span class="kbd">--color</span>, and let <span class="kbd">rumor docs --agent</span> teach an AI
          tool the whole config schema in one shot.</p>
        </FeatureRow>
      </div>

      <div class="feat-term">
        <TerminalDemo />
      </div>
    </section>

    <FeatureGrid />

    <section id="install" class="install-section" data-station="install" data-accent="running">
      <div class="container install-inner">
        <p class="eyebrow">get started</p>
        <h2 class="display install-title">One command and <span class="hl">you're running</span>.</h2>
        <p class="install-lead dim">macOS, Apple Silicon or Intel. No runtime, no daemon — a single
        static binary.</p>
        <div class="install-widget"><InstallTabs id="footer" /></div>
        <div class="install-cta">
          <a class="btn primary" href={REPO_URL} rel="noopener">Read the docs</a>
          <a class="btn" href={`${REPO_URL}/tree/main/rumor/examples/fullstack`} rel="noopener">See a full example</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
  <StatusBar />
</Base>

<style>
  .features {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.92fr) minmax(0, 1.08fr);
    gap: 0 56px;
    align-items: start;
    padding-top: 24px;
  }
  /* trailing room so the sticky terminal stays centered while the LAST row
     reaches viewport center, instead of bottoming out against the grid end. */
  .feat-stream { border-left: 1px solid var(--border-soft); padding-bottom: 14vh; }
  .feat-term {
    position: sticky;
    top: 70px;
    height: calc(100vh - var(--statusbar-h) - 92px);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .feat-term > :global(.term-wrap) { width: 100%; }

  .install-section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    margin-top: 56px;
    padding: clamp(44px, 9vw, 84px) 0 clamp(40px, 8vw, 72px);
    text-align: center;
  }
  .install-inner { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; }
  .install-inner .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .install-title { font-size: clamp(28px, 4.6vw, 52px); margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .install-title .hl { color: var(--running); }
  .install-lead { max-width: 500px; margin: 0 0 32px; font-size: 14px; }
  .install-widget { width: 100%; max-width: 700px; text-align: left; }
  .install-cta { display: flex; gap: 11px; margin-top: 28px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; }

  /* tablet: single column, terminal first, lightly pinned at the top */
  @media (max-width: 1024px) {
    .features { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0; }
    .feat-stream { border-left: none; padding-bottom: 0; min-width: 0; }
    .feat-term {
      order: -1;
      position: sticky;
      top: 54px;
      height: auto;
      z-index: 5;
      padding: 12px 0;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--bg) 82%, transparent);
    }
  }
  /* phone: terminal scrolls inline at the top, no pinning (mimics pi.dev) */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .feat-term {
      position: static;
      padding: 4px 0 8px;
      background: none;
    }
    .install-section { margin-top: 40px; }
  }
</style>
